findings.suggested_fix:
Translate or localize common bird names into standard contemporary Italian, or provide accepted Italian equivalents in parentheses after the English name. Preserve the original HTML and inline structure. Examples:
- killdeer → «killdeer (charadrius vociferus / pluvier vociante)» or if a common Italian name is preferred give the nearest equivalent «pluviero chiacchierino (killdeer)»;
- song sparrow → «song sparrow (passero canoro)» or «passero canoro (song sparrow)»;
- rose‑breasted grosbeak → «rose‑breasted grosbeak (cardinalide dal petto rosa)» or provide the Italian common name if available;
- wren → «cettia/zigolo» or the appropriate Italian common name, e.g. «regolo» for wren-like species;
- nightingale → «usignolo»;
- bunting → «zigolo/bunt» with specific Italian common name;
- cowbird → «cowbird (molothrus) / parasita dell’uccello»;
- starlings → «storni»;
- grackles → «grackles (quasi-simili al gracco)»;
- crow(s) → «corvo/i». 
(If the translator is unsure of an exact Italian common name, include the English name in parentheses after the Italian term.)
